InventoryTest
├── When anyone safely transfers a supported NFT
│   └── It should register custody without approval or a deposit call.
├── When anyone syncs an unsafe transfer
│   └── It should register it exactly once.
├── When a token is not held by the auction
│   └── It should revert.
├── When an unrelated collection is sent
│   └── It should revert.
├── When a receiver callback is forged
│   └── It should revert.
├── When an assigned prize is synced
│   └── It should revert.
├── When a claimed prize is safely returned
│   └── It should become eligible again without reopening its old claim.
├── When a claimed prize is unsafely returned
│   └── It should become eligible again only after sync.
├── When an NFT arrives at the cutoff
│   └── It should enter the following round only.
├── When an NFT arrives after randomness is known
│   └── It should leave the locked selection unchanged.
├── When a late arrival remains behind the next cutoff
│   └── It should preserve the eligible prefix through settlement.
├── When a raw transfer predates cutoff but sync follows it
│   └── It should use the registration time for eligibility.
├── When an empty day has only queued prizes
│   └── It should promote them without charging a bidder.
├── When unsold recovery is attempted while open
│   └── It should revert.
├── When a closed auction receives an unsafe transfer
│   └── It should permit sync and unsold recovery without reopening.
└── When a recipient attempts reentrancy while claiming
    └── It should reject registration inside the claim.
